# `pluss::subsp::stats::ts::ewm_std`

The exponentially weighted standard deviation of a series.

## Signature

```cpp
pluss::Series ts::ewm_std(const pluss::Series& x, double alpha, double epsilon = 1e-12);
```

## What It Does

`ewm_std` is the standard deviation matching [`ewm_mean`](ewm_mean.md): it uses the same geometrically falling weights and a running variance recursion, `v[t] = (1 − alpha) · (v[t − 1] + alpha · (x[t] − m[t − 1])²)` with `m` the [`ewm_mean`](ewm_mean.md), so no two large numbers are subtracted. The first position is 0, as a single observation has no spread. It is the exponentially weighted volatility of a return series.

## Parameters

`const pluss::Series& x`
: A one-dimensional series in time order. A series with more than one dimension is rejected.

`double alpha`
: The weight of the newest observation, in (0, 1]. A larger value forgets the past faster; `alpha = 1` returns the series unchanged. Values outside (0, 1] are rejected.

`double epsilon`
: A small floor on the variance so rounding can never produce a negative value under the square root (default 1e-12).

## Returns

A `Series` of the same length as `x`.

## Errors

- `alpha` outside (0, 1] is rejected.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The weighted standard deviation grows as the series becomes more variable.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>

#include <cmath>
#include <iomanip>
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

namespace ts = pluss::subsp::stats::ts;
using pluss::Series;

const auto f64 = pluss::Config{}.with_dtype(pluss::ScalarType::Float64);
void show(const char* label, const Series& s) {
  std::cout << std::left << std::setw(14) << label << std::right << std::fixed << std::setprecision(4);
  for (double v : s.host<double>()) std::cout << std::setw(9) << v;
  std::cout << "\n";
}

int main() {
  const Series x = pluss::make_series({10.0, 12.0, 11.0, 15.0, 14.0, 18.0, 17.0}, f64);
  show("x", x);
  show("ewm_std(x,.5)", ts::ewm_std(x, 0.5));
}
```

### Example 2

A constant series has zero spread everywhere.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>

#include <cmath>
#include <iomanip>
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

namespace ts = pluss::subsp::stats::ts;
using pluss::Series;

const auto f64 = pluss::Config{}.with_dtype(pluss::ScalarType::Float64);
void show(const char* label, const Series& s) {
  std::cout << std::left << std::setw(14) << label << std::right << std::fixed << std::setprecision(4);
  for (double v : s.host<double>()) std::cout << std::setw(9) << v;
  std::cout << "\n";
}

int main() {
  const Series x = pluss::make_series({5.0, 5.0, 5.0, 5.0}, f64);
  show("ewm_std", ts::ewm_std(x, 0.5));
}
```


